[{:adr/consequences "{:bug_fix \"individual org/repo pages not showing the game is fixed as a structural\\n            side effect of the architecture simplification, not a standalone patch --\\n            the class of bug (Worker silently missing/wrong) becomes impossible once\\n            routing is client-side\", :extensibility \"future game/stage/page additions become \\\"add a reagent view + a\\n                  route table entry\\\", no server-side routing file to update\", :migration_cost \"one-time port of play.html/dance.html/assets.html/generate.html/\\n                    studio.html's vanilla bootstrap logic into reagent lifecycles\\n                    without regressions; play_ai.cljs/segment_toggle.cljs already\\n                    reagent, least rework; isekai.stage.cljc's live-presence\\n                    (BroadcastChannel/WS) and play.html's kototama/kami-webgpu boot\\n                    sequence need care\", :canvas_ownership_convention \"canvas/WebGPU surface owned entirely by a\\n                                 :component-did-mount (reagent renders it once,\\n                                 kami-webgpu writes to it every frame, reagent never\\n                                 re-renders that subtree)\"}", :adr/authoritative_for ["gftdcojp/network-isekai's public/_worker.js does not exist on main (verified via\n    production HTTP behavior + git log --all) -- every /<org>/<game> pretty URL\n    (e.g. /gftd/drive) currently serves the marketing landing page instead of\n    play.html's game view" "the fix direction is NOT to resurrect _worker.js -- it is to consolidate to a\n    single reagent/re-frame SPA shell with client-side routing, formalize Cloudflare\n    Pages' already-observed 200-fallback-to-index.html via an explicit\n    `/* /index.html 200` _redirects rule, and retire the per-route static HTML +\n    server-side content-rewrite architecture entirely" "game/stage rendering loop (kotoba-lang/kami-engine + kami-webgpu, render-IR, WASM\n    compile) is unaffected by this ADR and stays as-is -- only the web/UI shell layer\n    is being unified onto reagent/re-frame"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by ["adr-2607022800-kotoba-lang-default-uiux-appkit-uikit-interface-fundamentals"], :adr/topic "network-isekai-spa-reagent", :adr/related ["90-docs/adr/2607032400-network-isekai-primary-consolidation.md"], :adr/status "superseded", :adr/addendum-2026-07-08-maturity-audit-superseded "{:trigger \"maturity audit re-checked this ADR's own Decision items against\\n            gftdcojp/network-isekai's origin/main @ b7388f1, after a prior pass had\\n            flagged it as still :proposed despite apparently substantial reagent\\n            work landing (commit 4cedf3e / PR #110)\", :finding [\"public/index.html, play.html, dance.html, assets.html, generate.html,\\n    studio.html are still six separate static HTML documents in production --\\n    no single SPA shell, no :view/route dispatch anywhere (grep -rn ':view'\\n    src/isekai/ finds only unrelated WebGPU texture-view keys); the reagent apps\\n    that do exist (src/isekai/ui/{app,db,events,subs,views,modes}.cljs) implement\\n    ADR-0003's separate multimode CAD/game/modeling/animation editor, not this\\n    ADR's page router\" \"the multi-document architecture was formalized further, not retired:\\n    src/isekai/site/build.cljc (`nbb render-site`) code-generates every\\n    public/*.html shell from its own .cljc source, citing ADR-2607022800 -- a\\n    different ADR (kotoba-lang UI/UX design system), not this one\" \"public/_redirects still lists explicit per-org-prefix rewrite rules\\n    (/gftd/* /play 200, /itonami/* /play 200, /studio/gftd/* /studio 200,\\n    /studio/itonami/* /studio 200) with a comment instructing future maintainers\\n    to add a line per new org -- exactly the manual-routing-config burden this\\n    ADR's :extensibility consequence set out to eliminate via a universal\\n    `/* /index.html 200` fallback, which does not exist\" \"the routing bug was fixed by PR #106 (`fix(routing): restore /<org>/<game>\\n    pretty-URL routing`, commit 1eeb2e6, branch feat/spa-reagent-consolidation)\\n    via those scoped per-org _redirects rules, not the universal client-router\\n    fallback this ADR called for; PR #106's own description states the\\n    play.html/dance.html/studio.html bootstraps were 'plain inline JS (not\\n    re-frame)' and isekai.web/isekai.stage were 'plain CLJS (direct DOM\\n    manipulation), not re-frame' at that point -- i.e. the multi-document,\\n    non-reagent architecture was deliberately kept\" \"commit 4cedf3e (PR #110, 'convert every page's UI chrome to reagent\\n    (ADR-2607022800)') converts each static page's widgets in place\\n    (rdom/render mounting status-view/editor-view/buttons-view into fixed DOM\\n    ids the still-separate static HTML documents declare -- see\\n    isekai/web.cljc:38-39 and isekai/stage.cljc:487-488, both commented\\n    'Mounted once at boot into <page>.html's static containers/ids') -- this\\n    satisfies ADR-2607022800's reagent-adoption mandate while implementing\\n    this ADR's own explicitly rejected Alternative 2 (multi-document\\n    architecture + reagent views inside each), not its actual spa_shell\\n    Decision\"], :disposition \"not retroactively implementing the spa_shell/router decision: the routing\\n   bug is already fixed in production (PR #106), the team has since invested\\n   further in the opposite direction (per-page codegen + widget-level reagent\\n   mounts, each with its own nbb.edn CI gate, under ADR-2607022800), and a\\n   repo-wide single-SPA rewrite of a live production site (isekai.network)\\n   would conflict with all of that subsequent work for uncertain benefit.\\n   Marked :superseded (by ADR-2607022800 for the reagent-adoption goal, by\\n   PR #106 for the routing-bug goal) rather than :accepted, since the\\n   architecture this ADR actually prescribed was never built.\", :known_remaining_gap \"public/_redirects still needs a manually-added line per new org namespace\\n   (2 total to date: gftd, itonami) -- the one concrete shortfall versus this\\n   ADR's stated :extensibility benefit. Left as an explicit, undone,\\n   low-value-at-current-scale follow-up rather than bundled into this audit.\"}", :adr/id "adr-2607041430-network-isekai-reagent-spa-consolidation", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-08", :adr/decision "{:spa_shell {:what \"collapse index.html/play.html/dance.html/assets.html/generate.html/\\n          studio.html into one SPA shell (single public/index.html, or the minimum\\n          shadow-cljs build output requires) mounting one reagent root\", :router \"client-side re-frame router reads window.location.pathname at boot,\\n            dispatches an event setting :view in app-db to one of\\n            :home | :play | :dance | :assets | :generate | :studio (+ :org/:game\\n            params for :play), generalizing the /<org>/<game> parsing already inline\\n            in play.html's boot script\"}, :view_migration {:play \"wrap the existing kototama-load + isekai.web/boot sequence in a reagent\\n          :component-did-mount / :component-will-unmount, replacing play.html's\\n          inline <script type=module>\", :dance \"wrap isekai.stage.cljc's loop the same way, replacing dance.html's direct\\n           DOM script; kami.dance/kami.webgpu render loop stays outside re-frame per\\n           deps.edn's existing UI-state/render-state split\", :home_assets_generate_studio \"become reagent components fed by re-frame subs,\\n                                   replacing current static-HTML + vanilla-script\\n                                   hydration\"}, :worker_js {:action \"NOT resurrected\", :replacement \"public/_redirects gets an explicit `/* /index.html 200` SPA-fallback\\n                 rule, formalizing the behavior Cloudflare Pages was already observed\\n                 applying by default -- every pretty URL serves the same SPA shell,\\n                 client router renders the right view, no server-side routing config\\n                 to keep in sync per new game/stage\"}, :stage_room_followup {:what \"wrangler.toml's StageRoom Durable Object (documented as living in the now-\\n          nonexistent public/_worker.js) needs a new home -- Cloudflare Pages Function\\n          under functions/, or the standalone-worker sketch already in wrangler.toml's\\n          comments\", :blocking false, :interim_behavior \"live-presence falls back to BroadcastChannel-only, the already-\\n                       documented behavior when /api/stage-room 501s\"}}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"user report: isekai.network individual org/repo pages (e.g. /gftd/drive)\\n            don't show the game\", :investigated [\"curl diff: https://isekai.network/gftd/drive returns 200 with content\\n    byte-identical to https://isekai.network/ (the marketing landing page); any\\n    nonexistent path (e.g. /totally-nonexistent-path-xyz123) returns the same;\\n    https://isekai.network/play alone correctly serves play.html's content\\n    (canvas/editor). All referenced static assets (kototama.js/.wasm, js/app.js,\\n    games/gftd/drive/{game.edn,logic.cljc,scene.edn}) individually return 200.\" \"public/_redirects' own comment says routing is handled by public/_worker.js; that\\n    file does not exist anywhere in main's history (git log --all -- public/_worker.js\\n    only finds it on `manifest-rev`, a branch never merged into main, and only in a\\n    commit that DELETES it). wrangler.toml still documents a StageRoom Durable Object\\n    class as living in that nonexistent file.\" \"network-isekai's web layer is several independent static HTML documents\\n    (index.html marketing LP, play.html editor, dance.html VRM stage, assets.html\\n    Asset Hub, generate.html, studio.html) glued together by that one Worker file --\\n    a single point of failure for every current and future game/stage route, silently\\n    broken with nothing catching it\" \"the web/UI layer is already partially reagent/re-frame (deps.edn: re-frame 1.4.3 +\\n    reagent 1.2.0; src/isekai/ui/{db,events,subs,views,app}.cljs is a standard\\n    re-frame split; segment_toggle.cljs / play_ai.cljs are reagent components mounted\\n    into specific DOM ids) but play.html's own inline boot script and\\n    dance.html/isekai.stage.cljc (defonce atom + raw getElementById/querySelector) are\\n    still vanilla DOM bootstraps\" \"user direction 2026-07-04: kami-engine/kami-webgpu render loop is architecturally\\n    correct and untouched; the web/UI layer should be reagent end-to-end (\\\"web部分は\\n    全画面をreagent\\\")\"], :risk \"network-isekai is a live production site (isekai.network) -- this is a\\n         cross-cutting web-layer migration touching every page's bootstrap, not an\\n         additive change. Canvas/WebGPU ownership must not fight reagent's virtual-DOM\\n         re-renders.\"}", :adr/alternatives "[{:option \"resurrect/rewrite public/_worker.js to restore the old per-route\\n            content-rewrite behavior\", :rejected_because \"treats the symptom, not the structural fragility -- one worker\\n                       file was a silent single point of failure for every existing\\n                       and future game route, and nothing caught it breaking; also\\n                       doesn't address the separate reagent-unification direction\"} {:option \"keep the multi-static-HTML-document architecture and add reagent views\\n            inside each independently\", :rejected_because \"doesn't fix the routing bug (still depends on a working Worker\\n                       to route to the right static document); keeps N separate\\n                       bootstrap entry points instead of one shell\"}]", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607041430: network-isekai — consolidate to a single reagent/re-frame SPA shell; retire per-route static HTML + the missing _worker.js"}]